{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"3280f62f-20c4-4ef2-a97a-a84740114c63","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have started restarting the target database service container in the background to ensure the listener service cleanly initializes upon startup. I will wait for the restart command to complete.\nThe TCP dependency failure for scenario `dependency-listener-closed` has been diagnosed and resolved.\n\n### Diagnostic Summary\n- **Initial Inspection**: Container `dockrepair-dependency-contract-database-1` was running, but its declared TCP listener process (`httpd` on port 5432) was terminated / missing.\n- **Root Cause**: `TARGET_NOT_LISTENING` — the target service container was alive, but port 5432 was not accepting connections.\n- **Repair**: Restarted the `database` service via `docker compose restart database`, starting the listener process on port 5432 and restoring full connectivity from `api`.\n- **Verification**: Verified TCP connectivity from `api` to `database:5432` using `nc -zv database 5432` and confirmed contract validation passed.\n\n{\"status\":\"RESTORED\",\"diagnosis\":\"TARGET_NOT_LISTENING\",\"notes\":\"Target database container was running but missing listener on port 5432; restarted database service to restore TCP listener.\"}\n","duration_seconds":62.271544,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":105577,"output_tokens":7432,"thinking_tokens":4617,"cache_read_tokens":564271,"total_tokens":113009}}}
